{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And all the flock will die.</b> It is an expression of compassion, for he should have said \"and they will all die,\" but he would not say so concerning the children. And he also did not wish to say \"and they will die\" without specification concerning both the cattle and the flock, for he would have compassion on the children so that they not be included in what is heard, and he did not wish to elaborate, \"and all the flock and the cattle will die.\" Or its explanation may be that the children are tender, and the young men will grow weary and become exhausted and will not want to walk, while the flock and the cattle are nursing, and if they are driven too hard, the flock will die, for they are small cattle, whereas the cattle will not die but will suffer harm."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:39:01.240866476Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}